-The high-level policy decides while neutral at reference ticks $k\in\{15,50,70\}$
-(0.30, 1.00 and 1.40 s). It may commit to a currently legal schedule or WAIT.
-After commitment, the qualified schedule controls holding and return; no second
-entry, adaptation-to-adaptation switch, arbitrary duration, stop or steering
-command is available. Different request phases can precede the same physical
-adaptation onset, so entry time alone is not a measured capability improvement.
-
-A six-second, 180-frame 30 Hz reference loads as 299 native 50 Hz samples. Each
-complete bounded episode records 298 synchronized control rows and 1,192 physics substeps.
-The last sensor capture is at elapsed 5.94 s, before the wrap callback. At a
-reference tick $k$, the preaction sensor packet is captured at $(k-1)/50$ s.
-Entry/return phases use the reference clock; passage time uses the physical
-recording clock.
-
-Passage requires initial approach upstream of every enabled beam, ordered full
-body-origin crossing and the registered 0.30 s stabilization hold, legal recovery,
-no fall/reset, and no disallowed environmental contact throughout the recorded
-horizon. Explicit body/counterpart forces are measured at 200 Hz; the registered
-contact limit is 1 N, with permitted foot--floor support and internal self-contact
-reported separately. A crossed finish with insufficient remaining hold is a
-finite-horizon task failure. An admitted early contact, fall or refusal can
-establish failure even when later supervision is unavailable; unverified outcomes
-remain unknown. Mechanical work is unavailable
-in this interface because applied actuator torque is not measured; it is stored
-as null. Teaching cost uses measured successful passage time, without an invented
-crouching or energy penalty. Specifically, passage time ends at crossing plus
-stabilization; success additionally requires recovery and acceptable contact
-through the remaining horizon. Thus a 2.72 s passage may precede a 5.30 s return
-phase. Passage time is not the duration of the complete adaptation--recovery
-maneuver, and does not measure readiness to begin a second adaptation.
-
-For each fixed task, $\max_s\mathbf1[\tau_s\text{ passes}]$ measures the capability
-of this finite bank. Actual policy completion additionally depends on choosing a
-usable schedule. A teacher search over all seven complete schedules establishes
-the bank's tested capability, not a globally optimal humanoid response.
