-\section{Limitations and Conclusion}
-Motion2Scene connects useful motion alternatives to training scenes through
-executed geometry, complete physical continuations and causal sensor evidence.
-The measured six-context bank contains complementary successful responses.
-Adding the complementary teaching data raises the learner from five to six
-successful development contexts, matching the retuned script while adding
-0.50 s on each of two earlier passages. The common-pool construction experiment
-also finds substantial reference-to-execution geometric disagreement. The
-completed M4 acquisition shows higher adaptation-required task yield for
-executed contrast, while each corpus remains solvable by a fixed schedule and
-its recorded branch-selection readout ties uniform. The central remaining test
-is whether execution-conditioned construction and
-causally usable supervision improve held-out traversal at matched acquisition
-cost; replay's additional contribution is tested separately.
-
-The current interface follows one finite route with at most one adaptation and
-recovery. It cannot stop, steer, select a route or chain repeated adaptations.
-Ideal ray normals, summarized rather than fully observed free space, reused
-source ancestry, nominal physical tests and a short fixed horizon limit the
-claims. Unknown torque prevents mechanical-work or battery-energy comparisons.
